    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      426.12,
      542.71,
      438.12
    ],
    "text": "The learned counsel for the Petitioner contends that the euisdem generis rule is engaged in the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      445.58,
      542.71,
      460.08
    ],
    "text": "instant matter and that the \"reimbursable allowance\" paid to the 3rd Respondent does not fall",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      470.04,
      542.71,
      482.04
    ],
    "text": "within the phrase \"cost of living allowance, special living allowance and other similar",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      491.94,
      302.41,
      503.94
    ],
    "text": "allowances\" in the above statutory provisions.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      523.98,
      542.71,
      535.98
    ],
    "text": "In Sohli Eduljee Captain v. Commissioner of Inland Revenue (77 N.L.R. 350 at 353) Wijayatilake J.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      545.94,
      542.71,
      557.94
    ],
    "text": "explained the scope of the ejusdem generis rule of construction in the interpretation of statutes",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      567.9,
      530.35,
      579.9
    ],
    "text": "by summing up Maxwell on the Interpretation of Statutes, 12th Ed., pp. 297 to 305 as follows:",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      599.88,
      542.71,
      611.88
    ],
    "text": "\"In the abstract, general words, like all others, receive their full and natural meaning,",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      621.9,
      542.71,
      633.9
    ],
    "text": "and the Courts will not impose on them limitations not called for by the sense or objects",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      643.86,
      542.71,
      655.86
    ],
    "text": "of the Enactment. But the general word which follows particular and specific words of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      665.82,
      542.71,
      677.82
    ],
    "text": "the same nature as itself takes its meaning from them and is presumed to be restricted",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      687.78,
      542.71,
      699.78
    ],
    "text": "to the same genus as those words. For according to a well established rule, in the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      731.33,
      542.48,
      755.74
    ],
    "text": "Page 4 of 5",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.979999542236328
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      74.4,
      542.71,
      86.4
    ],
    "text": "construction of Statutes, general terms following particular ones apply only to such",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      96.36,
      542.71,
      108.36
    ],
    "text": "persons or things as are ejusdem generis with those comprehended in the language of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      118.32,
      542.71,
      130.32
    ],
    "text": "the Legislature. In other words, the general expression is to be read as comprehending",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      140.34,
      542.71,
      152.34
    ],
    "text": "only things of the same kind as that designated by the preceding particular expressions,",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      162.3,
      542.71,
      174.3
    ],
    "text": "unless there is something to show that a wider sense was intended as where there is a",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      184.26,
      542.71,
      196.26
    ],
    "text": "provision specifically excepting certain classes clearly not within the suggested",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      206.22,
      542.71,
      218.22
    ],
    "text": "genus\u2026The rule applies only to general words following words which are less general.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      228.18,
      542.71,
      240.18
    ],
    "text": "Unless there is a genus or class or category, there is no room for any application of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      250.2,
      542.71,
      262.2
    ],
    "text": "ejusdem generis doctrine\u2026The rule of ejusdem generis may apply despite the absence of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      108.0,
      272.1,
      387.31,
      284.1
    ],
    "text": "the word 'other' at the end of the list of things specified.\"",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      304.14,
      542.71,
      316.14
    ],
    "text": "It is notable that the first two words refer to two types of living allowances namely cost of living",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      326.1,
      542.71,
      338.1
    ],
    "text": "allowance and special living allowance. The genus is \"living allowance\" and accordingly the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      348.06,
      542.71,
      360.06
    ],
    "text": "words \"other similar allowances\" must be interpreted to cover only different varieties of living",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      370.02,
      542.71,
      382.02
    ],
    "text": "allowances. This is confirmed by the use of the words \"other similar\" and the fact that the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      392.04,
      542.71,
      404.04
    ],
    "text": "definition uses the word \"means\" which is indicative of a definition that is restrictive in nature",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      414.0,
      542.71,
      426.0
    ],
    "text": "and exhaustive. Therefore, for any allowance to fall within the phrase \"other similar",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      435.9,
      325.33,
      447.9
    ],
    "text": "allowances\" it must be a type of a living allowance.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      465.44,
      542.71,
      479.94
    ],
    "text": "The 3rd Respondent did not claim that it was a type of a living allowance. The position of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      487.39,
      542.71,
      501.9
    ],
    "text": "Petitioner is that the \"allowance\" paid to the 3rd Respondent was a reimbursable allowance",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      511.86,
      542.71,
      523.86
    ],
    "text": "intended to cover the expenses incurred in entertaining customers and other expenses incurred",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      533.82,
      437.71,
      545.82
    ],
    "text": "as part of his travel island wide to promote the products of the Petitioner.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      563.3,
      542.71,
      577.8
    ],
    "text": "The 3rd Respondent, in affidavit dated 2nd April 2014 (2R5) submitted to the Department of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      587.82,
      542.71,
      599.82
    ],
    "text": "Labour, has claimed that at the time of termination of services, his salary was Rs. 2,00,000/= of",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      609.78,
      542.71,
      621.78
    ],
    "text": "which Rs. 125000/= and Rs. 75,000/= were paid at two different times. He further states that he",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      631.74,
      542.71,
      643.74
    ],
    "text": "was paid a special allowance of Rs. 9000/= from September 2006 which was increased to",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      653.7,
      542.71,
      665.7
    ],
    "text": "15,000/= in October 2008. A further increase to Rs. 35,000/= was made April 2009 which was",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      675.66,
      542.71,
      687.66
    ],
    "text": "again increased to Rs. 40,000/= in June 2009. In September 2009 it was increased to Rs.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      731.33,
      542.48,
      755.74
    ],
    "text": "Page 5 of 5",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri-Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.979999542236328
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      74.4,
      542.71,
      86.4
    ],
    "text": "60,000/= and was again increased to Rs. 75,000/= in September 2011 and remained so until his",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      96.3,
      211.45,
      108.3
    ],
    "text": "termination in March 2013.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      128.34,
      542.71,
      140.34
    ],
    "text": "The Commissioner of Labour had first appointed an inquiring officer who after due inquiry",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      147.8,
      542.71,
      162.3
    ],
    "text": "concluded that the \"reimbursable allowance\" was in fact part of the wages or salary of the 3rd",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      172.32,
      542.71,
      184.32
    ],
    "text": "Respondent (2R6). Thereafter, this decision was informed to the Petitioner who submitted an",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      194.28,
      542.71,
      206.28
    ],
    "text": "appeal. The Commissioner of Labour then appointed another inquiring officer to look into the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      216.24,
      542.71,
      228.24
    ],
    "text": "matter. After inquiry that inquiring officer concluded that the \"reimbursable allowance\" can be",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      238.14,
      438.85,
      250.14
    ],
    "text": "considered as \"other allowance\" within the meaning of the EPF Act (2R10).",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      270.18,
      542.71,
      282.18
    ],
    "text": "As pointed out above, the term \"wages\" and \"other similar allowance\" have different meanings",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      289.64,
      542.71,
      304.14
    ],
    "text": "in the EPF Act. Therefore, the two inquiring officers appointed by the 1st Respondent came to",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      314.1,
      542.71,
      326.1
    ],
    "text": "two different conclusions although one may argue that it does not matter since both situations",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      336.12,
      542.71,
      348.12
    ],
    "text": "fall within the term \"earnings\" in the EPF Act. Yet, the second inquiring officer concludes that it",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      358.08,
      542.71,
      370.08
    ],
    "text": "falls within \"other allowance\" without any consideration of whether it is a type of a living",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      379.98,
      126.97,
      391.98
    ],
    "text": "allowance.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      409.52,
      542.71,
      424.02
    ],
    "text": "Confronted with these two inconsistent conclusions the 1st Respondent yet decided the",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      433.98,
      542.71,
      445.98
    ],
    "text": "\"reimbursable allowance\" to be within the meaning of \"earnings\" in the EPF Act. That in my",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      453.38,
      406.87,
      467.88
    ],
    "text": "opinion is arbitrary and ulta vires the powers of the 1st Respondent.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.980000019073486,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      487.92,
      542.71,
      499.92
    ],
    "text": "For all the foregoing reasons, I issue writs of certiorari quashing the decisions contained in",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      509.82,
      516.85,
      521.82
    ],
    "text": "letters dated 22.12.2015 (P15), 23.10.2014 (P8 (a)), 30.10.2014 (P8) and 16.12.2014 (P13).",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 4,
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      541.8,
      326.71,
      553.8
    ],
    "text": "The parties shall bear their costs.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
